# 1v1, the whole field on MOVE-28 stop-and-start (BENCH-208). pc-tailor-field's screen (PR #686) switched each lever on
# for every robot; hj was the only one that read better than master over the whole field: +0.26 +/- 0.16 APS at 2 seeds
# (bands 3-6 all positive, band 6, the 511 weakest robots, +0.30 +/- 0.11). That was one 2-seed look. This card measures
# it again on fresh seeds against master and its A/A copy, with the per-robot picks of pc-tailor-field and
# pc-tailor-near already in master, before hj is shipped for the field.
# Leigh starts it once the PC is free (after pc-tailor-near; one card at a time, from master):
#   git checkout master && git pull
#   .\queue.ps1 run pc-hj-field        (or  ./queue.sh run pc-hj-field)
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, unpinned, 12 workers, truth log off. Every step resumes; no step needs a
# decision. Size: 1,212 robots x 3 arms (c, aa, hj) x 3 seeds = 10,908 battles, ~15-17 h at ~650-750 battles/h; the
# pilot is every fifth robot (~243) at the same seeds, the first fifth of the run (~3 h), and the field resumes it.
#
# Why it should win (the PC card rule of 2026-11-03; Leigh chose this card on 2026-11-07, "Both, near misses first"):
#   - Per-opponent tailoring taken to the whole field: hj is a per-robot table switch (heat-jit: lines, MOVE-28), duel
#     only, so team and melee are unchanged; this card asks whether every robot of the field should carry it.
#   - Measured: on pc-tailor-field's screen hj was +0.26 +/- 0.16 APS over 1,194 robots; every other lever was flat or
#     negative there (x5 -0.17, mm -0.13). Its gain is spread thin over the weak and mid field, the place the 5-point
#     per-robot margin cannot see.
#   - The mechanism (MOVE-13): the surf takes each tick's newest movement wave, the enemy's gun-heat wave included, as
#     its provisional wave instead of holding one, so it starts dodging a shot the moment the enemy's gun can fire,
#     not once the shot is seen; robots that fire as soon as their gun is cool are dodged earlier.
#   - Risk: hj ships only if it clears +0.03 APS with its 95% low end above 0 on these fresh seeds, pooled against c
#     and aa; the per-robot report then names the robots it costs, which stay off the list.
# Pilot (stop rule): every fifth robot of the field that loads (work/panel-hjf-pilot.txt; broken-1.11.2.txt's robots are
#   left out first, since the bench drops them and the pilot needs every robot it names) x c, aa, hj x 3 seeds from 9700. When
#   hj's mean gain over c and aa there is below 0, work/hjf.stop is written, every later step skips and the results PR
#   carries the pilot alone.
# field: census-312.txt x c, aa, hj x 3 seeds from 9700 (the pilot's battles are kept); gate +0.03 APS over the field.
# Stop rules (docs/bench/watch.md): halt on 30 failed battles, an arm scoring nothing in 8, 90+ skipped turns a battle
# over the last 200, or no battle in 30 minutes; every battle fought is kept and a rerun resumes. Nothing here ships:
# the heat-jit lines go into ShieldTableData by PR; the release rule stands.

set V = 3.21
set P = --parallel 12 --no-truth-log --failed-ok
set C = --skip-build --skip-fetch --rounds 35 --cpu-constant 1488498 --child-heap 2G
set W = work/hjf
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin

prep | git checkout -q master && mkdir -p bisect work && rm -f work/hjf.stop && (cd .. && mvn -q -DskipTests package) && cp ../hadur-robot/target/hadur117.Hadur_${V}.jar bisect/ && grep -v '^#' census-312.txt | cut -d'|' -f1 | sed 's/ *$//' | grep . > work/field.list && awk -F'|' '{gsub(/\r/, "")} /^#/ || !NF {next} {n = $1; gsub(/^ +| +$/, "", n); gsub(/ +/, " ", n)} NR == FNR {b[n] = 1; next} !(n in b) && k++ % 5 == 0' broken-1.11.2.txt census-312.txt > work/panel-hjf-pilot.txt && bash ./build-ablation.sh aa && HEAT_JIT=work/field.list bash ./build-ablation.sh hjlist && test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}aa.jar && test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}hl.jar && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set census-312.txt && mvn -q compile

pilot | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set work/panel-hjf-pilot.txt --seeds 3 --seed-base 9700 --arms plans/hj-field.arms --out ${W} --label hjf --shuffle-jobs && python3 tools/x5_card.py pilot ${W}/arms.tsv --names work/panel-hjf-pilot.txt --check hj=work/panel-hjf-pilot.txt@0 --ref c,aa --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_hjf-pilot.md --stop-file work/hjf.stop
  after: prep
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: skips 90 over 200
  stop: stall 30m

field | if [ -f work/hjf.stop ]; then echo 'pilot: hj below master on the pilot robots, no field run'; exit 0; fi && ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set census-312.txt --seeds 3 --seed-base 9700 --arms plans/hj-field.arms --out ${W} --label hjf --shuffle-jobs
  after: pilot
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: skips 90 over 200
  stop: stall 30m

gate | if [ -f work/hjf.stop ]; then echo 'stopped (see work/hjf.stop): skipped'; exit 0; fi && python3 ../data/tools/multiarm.py ${W}/arms.tsv --census census-312.txt --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_hjf.md && python3 tools/shield_s2.py gate ${W}/arms.tsv --arm hj --panel census-312.txt --bar 0.03 --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_hjf-gate.md && python3 tools/per_robot.py ${W}/arms.tsv --arms hj --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_hjf-per-robot.md --out-tsv ${OUT}/hjf-per-robot.tsv
  after: field

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-hj-field-results "1v1 whole field: MOVE-28 stop-and-start for every robot, fresh seeds" ${OUT}/*_hjf*.md $(find ${OUT} -maxdepth 1 -name 'hjf*.tsv' -size +0c)
  after: gate
